(373, 4, 'What is the name of the student in the story?', 'Text: Sokha’s Preparation\n\nSokha is a high school student who has just finished his final exam. He lives in a small town with his parents and older sister. Every morning, Sokha wakes up early to help his mother at home. Then he spends time reading books about different jobs and skills. He wants to enter vocational school after high school because he believes practical skills are very important for the future.\n\nSokha is interested in tourism and hospitality. He thinks that vocational education will help him learn how to serve customers, communicate in English, and manage events. He knows that many hotels and restaurants are looking for skilled workers, so studying at vocational school can give him better job opportunities.\n\nAfter lunch, Sokha usually practices English and math because they are useful for his future study. In the evening, he talks with his father about different careers. His father tells him that having a skill is like having a key to many doors. On weekends, Sokha visits his cousin who already studies at a vocational school. His cousin shows him some projects, like preparing menus and welcoming guests. Sokha feels excited and motivated.\n\nSokha dreams of becoming a professional in the hospitality industry and supporting his family. He understands that vocational education can give him both knowledge and real experience. His family is proud of him and encourages him to follow his dream.', 0, 1, '2026-09-30 08:09:37', '2026-09-30 08:09:37'),
